💡 **SUGGESTION: the kill-switch branch of `_shellToolDescription` is untested**

The conditional sentence is behavior the model consumes: armed →
"...still running after Ns is also moved to a background job
automatically..."; `Duration.zero` → absent ("the model must not be taught
the conversion it will never get", per the comment). Neither branch has a
test — the new suite covers the runtime behavior but never asserts the
description. Two cheap assertions close the gap:

```dart
test('bash description teaches the conversion only when armed', () {
  final armed = shellTool(env, jobs: registry,
      autoBackgroundAfter: _conversionThreshold);
  expect(armed.description, contains('moved to a background job'));
  final killed = shellTool(env, jobs: registry,
      autoBackgroundAfter: Duration.zero);
  expect(killed.description, isNot(contains('moved to a background job')));
});
```

