# Thread 3 — `lib/src/tools/builtin_tools_bash.dart:788` — supervisor anchor breaks when a rewrite notice precedes the conversion text

**Fixed** (the reviewer's second suggested option — skip a leading notice prefix — chosen over `contains`, for the reason the thread itself supplies).

`_isBackgroundHandback` (`lib/src/agent/agent_loop_stuck_supervision.dart`) now skips exactly ONE leading `[bash interceptor rewrote …]\n` notice line before the `startsWith(stuckBackgroundHandbackSentence)` anchor check:

```dart
final _interceptorNoticeLine = RegExp(
  r'^\[bash interceptor rewrote [^\n]*\]\n',
);

bool _isBackgroundHandback(ToolExecutionResult result) {
  if (_resultOutputSize(result) <= 0) return false;
  final text = _resultPartialText(result, max: 1 << 20).replaceFirst(
    _interceptorNoticeLine,
    '',
  );
  return text.startsWith(stuckBackgroundHandbackSentence);
}
```

Why prefix-skip and not `text.contains(...)`: the thread quotes the gh-1054 round-2 invariant — *a retry that merely QUOTES the hand-back text must not be audited as a conversion*. `contains` would break that protection (any mid-body quote would classify); the bounded prefix skip preserves it — the anchor stays positional, so ordinary output leading a quoted sentence still fails recognition.

Coverage (both consumers of the predicate):
- `test/agent/foreground_call_budget_test.dart` — "a rewrite-notice-prefixed hand-back still classifies as a background conversion (gh-1835 review)": budget ladder lands `ForegroundBudgetAction.background` for the prefixed result (before the fix it misclassified as an ordinary completion).
- `test/agent/stuck_tool_test.dart` — "a hand-back carrying a leading rewrite notice is still marked as a background conversion (gh-1835 review)": the supervisor reclassifies with the `backgroundConvert` mark.
- Negative guards kept green: the existing gh-1054 round-2 test (quoted mention ≠ conversion) and a new "anchor sentence quoted mid-body … is still not a conversion under the rewrite-notice skip" test.

The same pattern in `_backgroundHandbackResult` (steering hand-back) needs no producer-side change: the classifier fix covers both producers in one place.

# Thread 4 — `lib/src/tools/builtin_tools_bash.dart:247` — kill-switch branch of `_shellToolDescription` untested

**Fixed** — the suggested test now exists in `test/tools/bash_auto_background_test.dart`, group `bash tool description (gh-1835 review)`:

```dart
test('teaches the conversion only when armed', () {
  final armed = shellTool(env, jobs: registry,
      autoBackgroundAfter: _conversionThreshold);
  expect(armed.description, contains('moved to a background job automatically'));
  final killed = shellTool(env, jobs: registry,
      autoBackgroundAfter: Duration.zero);
  expect(killed.description,
      isNot(contains('moved to a background job automatically')));
});
```

One deliberate adjustment to the suggested assertion: the plain phrase `moved to a background job` also appears in the **pre-existing** soft-yield sentence ("A foreground command that is still running when the user sends a message is moved to a background job untouched (never killed)…"), which stays on the kill switch too. The test therefore anchors on the conversion sentence's unique phrase `moved to a background job automatically` — the literal suggested assertion would have failed for the wrong reason (the RED run proved exactly that). The intent is unchanged: armed teaches the conversion, `Duration.zero` does not.

